      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "Given a nine-sided regular polygon \\(A_1A_2A_3A_4A_5A_6A_7A_8A_9\\), we need to determine the number of distinct equilateral triangles formed by vertices that lie on the nine-sided polygon, with at least two vertices in the set \\(\\{A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_9\\}\\).\n\nFirst, consider the central angles of the nine-sided polygon. Since the polygon is regular, each internal angle is:\n\\[\n\\frac{(9-2)\\times 180^\\circ}{9} = 140^\\circ\n\\]\nThe central angles of the polygon are:\n\\[\n\\frac{360^\\circ}{9} = 40^\\circ\n\\]\nWe need to find the number of equilateral triangles formed by choosing vertices from the nine-sided polygon. An equilateral triangle with vertices \\(A_i, A_j, A_k\\) must satisfy:\n\\[\n|A_i - A_j| = |A_j - A_k| = |A_k - A_i| = 3\n\\]\nThis means that the central angle between any two chosen vertices must be \\(120^\\circ\\) (since \\(120^\\circ/40^\\circ = 3\\)).\n\nWe will count the number of such equilateral triangles in two cases: when two vertices lie on the polygon, and when all three vertices lie on the polygon.\n\n### Case 1: Two vertices lie on the polygon\nIf two vertices lie on the polygon, the third vertex must be \\(120^\\circ\\) away from the first vertex and then another \\(120^\\circ\\) away from the second vertex. This forms an equilateral triangle. The number of ways to choose 2 vertices out of 9 is \\(\\binom{9}{2}\\):\n\\[\n\\binom{9}{2} = 36\n\\]\n\n### Case 2: All three vertices lie on the polygon\nIf all three vertices lie on the polygon, the third vertex must be \\(120^\\circ\\) away from the first and then another \\(120^\\circ\\) away from the second in a clockwise direction. This is a group of three consecutive vertices on the polygon, which is one specific triangle for each vertex. There are 9 such triangles since there are 9 vertices.\n\nAdding the number of triangles from both cases, we get:\n\\[\n36 + 9 = 45\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the number of distinct equilateral triangles in the plane of the polygon that have at least two vertices in the set \\(\\{A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_9\\}\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{45}\n\\]",
